From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:02:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] client: retry definitive mutation conflicts with
 bounded policy

Retain completed HTTP failures as typed evidence and classify explicit pre-execution rejections. Retry public HTTP mutations only after a complete structured HTTP 503 OptimisticConcurrencyControlFailure response with a string message. Transport loss, incomplete bodies and UDF or arbitrary error text do not prove a write failed to commit.

Keep the existing configurable retry budget and delay. Action callbacks explicitly retain their established terminal-conflict message classifier. Cover physical attempt counts and preserve original errors for ambiguous outcomes.
